From: Kristianaaron <25537000+Kristianaaron@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tegra: accept canonical NVIDIA block-linear modifiers (page kind 0xfe)

drm_fourcc.h defines the legacy 16Bx2 block-linear modifiers, which encode
page kind 0, as the same layouts as the canonical modifiers with page kind
0xfe (drm_fourcc_canonicalize_nvidia_format_mod()). NVIDIA's GPU stack on
Tegra produces the canonical form; tegra-drm accepts only the legacy one, so
a compositor finds no common block-linear modifier and the only shared one,
LINEAR, cannot be rendered to by that stack.

Map the canonical kind back to the legacy form when reading a framebuffer's
tiling (the display engine does not use the page kind), and advertise the
canonical modifiers on Tegra124 and later planes.

STATUS (2026-11-19): NOT applied to linux-nano. Tested once as an
out-of-tree module: buffers then flowed from NVIDIA's stack to tegra-drm and
the kernel hit page-allocator corruption seconds later
(results/cuda/g2-20261119-0209-page-corruption-oops-netconsole.log). The
corruption is most likely in the nvmap dma-buf export path this patch first
exercised, not in this patch, but that is unproven.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git i/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/dc.c w/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/dc.c
index 0b3fcc701..41782319c 100644
--- i/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/dc.c
+++ w/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/dc.c
@@ -711,6 +711,13 @@ static const u64 tegra124_modifiers[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_16BX2_BLOCK(3),
 	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_16BX2_BLOCK(4),
 	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_16BX2_BLOCK(5),
+	/* the same layouts in canonical form (page kind 0xfe), as used by NVIDIA's GPU stack */
+	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_BLOCK_LINEAR_2D(0, 0, 0, 0xfe, 0),
+	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_BLOCK_LINEAR_2D(0, 0, 0, 0xfe, 1),
+	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_BLOCK_LINEAR_2D(0, 0, 0, 0xfe, 2),
+	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_BLOCK_LINEAR_2D(0, 0, 0, 0xfe, 3),
+	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_BLOCK_LINEAR_2D(0, 0, 0, 0xfe, 4),
+	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_BLOCK_LINEAR_2D(0, 0, 0, 0xfe, 5),
 	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID
 };
 
diff --git i/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fb.c w/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fb.c
index 0a7cb9e46..f319135b2 100644
--- i/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fb.c
+++ w/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fb.c
@@ -46,6 +46,16 @@ int tegra_fb_get_tiling(struct drm_framebuffer *framebuffer,
 			tiling->sector_layout = TEGRA_BO_SECTOR_LAYOUT_GPU;
 
 		modifier &= ~DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_SECTOR_LAYOUT;
+
+		/*
+		 * Page kind 0xfe ("generic" single-sample uncompressed color) is the
+		 * canonical form of the legacy 16Bx2 block-linear modifiers, which
+		 * encode it as 0 (see drm_fourcc_canonicalize_nvidia_format_mod()).
+		 * The display engine does not use the page kind: map the canonical
+		 * form back to the legacy one.
+		 */
+		if ((modifier & 0x10) && ((modifier >> 12) & 0xff) == 0xfe)
+			modifier &= ~(0xffULL << 12);
 	}
 
 	switch (modifier) {
